    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0236",
      "sequence": 248,
      "meaning": "‘By serving you the four aims are easily gained, boon-giving beloved of Śiva. Gods, humans and sages all become happy by worshipping your lotus feet. You know my desire well, Mother; you dwell forever in every heart-city. For that very reason I have not stated it openly.’ Saying this, Vaidehī clasped her feet. Bhavānī was overcome by her loving entreaty: the garland slipped down and the image smiled. Sītā reverently placed the gracious gift on her head, and Gaurī spoke, her heart filled with joy: ‘Hear, Sītā, my blessing is true—your heart’s desire will be fulfilled. Nārada’s word is ever pure and true; you will receive the very bridegroom on whom your mind is fixed.’",
