    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0240",
      "sequence": 252,
      "meaning": "‘Let us go to see Sītā’s self-choice; let us see to whom the Lord grants distinction.’ Lakṣmaṇa replied, ‘Only that person upon whom your grace rests, lord, is worthy of glory.’ All the sages rejoiced at his excellent words, blessed him and took delight. The compassionate Lord then went with the gathering of sages to see the bow-sacrifice hall. When the two brothers reached the arena, the news spread among all the townspeople. Forgetting every household task, children, youths, elders, men and women set out. Seeing the immense crowd, Janaka called all the orderly attendants and commanded: ‘Go at once to every person and give each a fitting seat.’ With humble, gentle words they seated the men and women—highest, middle, lowest and small—each according to their proper place.",
